# Day 08 – Group Policy Preferences (GPP) & Drive Mapping

## 🎯 Purpose
Automate the configuration of the user environment by seamlessly delivering network resources (like shared folders and printers) directly to the end-user's workstation at logon.

---

## 🔑 Key Concepts & Terms

* Group Policy Preferences (GPP): An extension of Group Policy that allows administrators to configure, deploy, and manage OS settings that were previously handled by complex logon scripts.
* Drive Mapping: The process of assigning a local drive letter (e.g., `H:`) to a remote network share (e.g., `\\dc01\HR-Docs`).
* Update Action: The standard GPP action that creates a mapped drive if it does not exist, or updates its settings if it has been modified.
* Replace Action: Deletes the existing mapped drive and recreates it from scratch (often used to clear out old, stuck connections).

---

## 🏗️ Architecture: GPO vs GPP

```text
GROUP POLICY (The Law)                  GROUP POLICY PREFERENCES (The Guide)
+------------------------+              +--------------------------+
| - Enforces Security    |              | - Delivers Resources     |
| - Cannot be changed    |              | - User can modify local  |
|   by the end-user.     |              |   settings if allowed.   |
| - e.g., Block Control  |              | - e.g., Map network      |
|   Panel, Force Lock.   |              |   drives, Add printers.  |
+------------------------+              +--------------------------+
```

