## ❓ Essential Interview Questions

Q1: Why do we use Group Policy Preferences for drive mapping instead of the old method of writing batch (.bat) logon scripts?
A1: GPP is built directly into Windows, processes much faster than scripts, provides a clean GUI for administrators, and allows for "Item-Level Targeting" (applying a drive map based on security groups rather than just OUs).

Q2: What is the UNC path format?
A2: Universal Naming Convention. It is formatted as `\\ServerName\ShareName`.

Q3: If a GPO is linked to the Domain level but applies User Configuration settings, will it affect the Administrator account?
A3: Yes. Unless explicitly filtered out, user policies apply to any user account residing inside the container (or child containers) where the GPO is linked.